codex
I found a more promising dim=384 path change: the non-128 projection path stores `out_gate` after sigmoid, then the final kernel reads it. Since the original `proj` buffer already contains the pre-sigmoid out gate, we can skip the post-kernel out-gate store and have the final kernel read from `proj` and apply sigmoid there, rounded back to fp16 to match the old path. This removes one large write from the 384 path.
apply patch
